<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Alexios I of Trebizond</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1182–1222</span> · <a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a> · Also known as Alexios I Megas Komnenos</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Alexios I was the founder of the Empire of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/trabzon">Trebizond</a>. A grandson of the emperor Andronikos I Komnenos, he seized Trebizond in 1204 with his brother <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/david">David</a> and Georgian troops supplied by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tamar-of-georgia">Queen Tamar</a>, just as the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fourth-crusade">Fourth Crusade</a> took <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/constantinople">Constantinople</a>. He took the imperial title and founded the dynasty of the Grand Komnenoi.</p></div>
